id: pmc-3jq8
title: Keep branch-only completions out of release tags that do not contain them
description: "pm-cli PR 1228 closed four items on a feature branch before the daily v2026.9.10 tag was cut from main. pm-changelog 2026.9.9 places those items in the released 2026.9.10 window solely from completed_at even though their terminal item state is absent from the tag. Verify git tag membership in the package-owned CLI and extension, preserve explicit release attribution and non-git SDK inputs, and retain untagged work until an actual release contains it."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: bug,changelog,git-tags,release
created_at: "2026-09-10T08:15:12.708Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-10T08:32:40.147Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-10T08:32:39.715Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-10T08:32:39.715Z"
author: codex
acceptance_criteria: A branch closure preceding a main release remains Unreleased until a tag includes it; the first containing release owns it across future regenerations; explicit release metadata and non-git callers remain compatible; CLI and extension share the SDK implementation; real temporary Git fixtures and complete quality gates pass
parent: pmc-qm7s
resolution: Added a shared Git tag membership resolver for live CLI and extension full-history generation; branch-only completions move to the first containing release or Unreleased while explicit release declarations remain authoritative.
expected_result: Release history must not attribute branch work to a tag that predates its integration; later runs must preserve the first containing release and malformed evidence must fail closed.
actual_result: "472 tests passed with 100 percent line/branch/function coverage and complete docstrings; real multi-branch and later-tag fixtures pass, and the native pm-cli consumer retains all 2351 entries while correcting nine early timestamp attributions."
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
